    {
      "question": "e-301",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "4163b192330f792db0317e4c0cde0ed2d188314a3f6bf4343e3026ee6698e039",
      "new_sha256": "f465f204de9b136e2fca7d518f64f07978fed0052dcb402aedc0e000ad87487d",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-301",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\dfrac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac{\\sin^2 (2x)}{x^2} &= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac {\\left[\\sin^2 (2x)\\right]'}{[x^2]'}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{2\\cdot \\sin (2x) \\cdot\\cos (2x)\\cdot 2}{2x}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}{2\\cos (2x)} \\cdot \\lim_{x\\to 0} \\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\cos(2\\cdot 0)\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\n}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\dfrac{0}{0}.$ But that's okay, because we can just apply L'Hopital's rule again! We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac{\\sin^2 (2x)}{x^2} &= 2\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=  2\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac {[\\sin (2x)]'}{[x]'}\\[5pt]\n&=  2\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac {2\\cos (2x)}{1}\\[5pt]\n&= 4\\cos(2\\cdot 0)\\\n&=4.\n}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-301.json",
          "file_sha256": "0240bd5760ae0f49edcc6a7c9fc2e6f9761a534c0714533e0c12d51dd544327a"
        }
      ],
