          "question": "e-303",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\dfrac{\\infty}{\\infty},$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {x^6}{5x^6-4} &= \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}  \\dfrac {[x^6]'}{[5x^6-4]'}\\\n&= \\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {6x^5}{5(6x^5)-0}\\\n&=  \\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {1}{5}\\\n&= \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n}\n$$",
